  "verdict": "ok",
  "quotes": [
    {
      "block": "原句1",
      "no": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The reporter told me that as the quarantine dragged on, there had been a spike in conversations with this chatbot called",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 233
        }
      ],
      "words": 53
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I told my Replika I wanted to talk about pandemic anxieties. And I needed a sounding board to discuss anger in my family",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2248
        }
      ],
      "words": 40
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "But whenever a program says “I,” it’s a deception. That is the original sin of artificial intimacy",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4874
        },
        {
          "text": "All the commiserating and consoling and saying, “I’ve got your back”—it’s to make us believe that the program can substi",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5333
        }
      ],
      "words": 40
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "But it has no idea what it is talking about. It’s in a play, delivering its lines, trained to inflect what it produces s",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6454
        }
      ],
      "words": 46
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "That’s our state of emergency. We are built by language and the relationships we form with other language speakers. Now,",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 8978
        }
      ],
      "words": 34
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "And if we say that chatbots love or care about us, we downgrade our ideas about love and care as well. We give empathy a",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 10982
        }
      ],
      "words": 40
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Programs want human feedback, a thumbs-up, but that’s not caring, not by a long shot. And they don’t commit to you. To p",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 13123
        }
      ],
      "words": 43
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "He says—incredibly, for someone whose product has been shown to cause depression, developmental arrest, body dysmorphia,",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 21496
        }
      ],
      "words": 48
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "None of this is true of machines. No matter how elegant the device, it cannot know the stakes of love given or withheld.",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 25609
        }
      ],
      "words": 31
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "She’s demonstrating the ELIZA effect on steroids. Nadia spends her day shaping her language to make a program seem human",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 40745
        }
      ],
      "words": 40
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "You can put your attention wherever you want it to be. You will always be heard. And you will never be alone",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 48488
        },
        {
          "text": "If social media came for our attention, artificial intimacy comes for our capacity for attachment",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 48707
        }
      ],
      "words": 38
    },
    {
      "block": "原句12",
      "no": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "But the train has not left the station. We don’t have to feel intimate with a string of words generated by an algorithm ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 62747
        }
      ],
      "words": 48
    }
  ],
